# HomerView
#
# Logs are written on every run and say nothing a reader of the repository
# needs. They are also the one file most likely to carry a local path.
*.log

# Generated at run time, all of them rewritten on the next run.
Axe.json
Ace.json
Report.html
Report.txt
Start.html
MainContent.htm
HomerView.db
HomerView.jsonl

# Private correspondence. Drafts live outside the repository.
Letter_to_*.md
Reply_to_*.md
Announcing_*.md
Announcing_*.htm
Letter_to_*.htm

# Python and build output.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
dist/

# Executables ARE tracked, deliberately. A user who clones this repository
# should be able to build the installer without hunting for pieces, and the
# built add-on and installer are part of what a release is.
!*.exe
!build/*.nvda-addon

# One exception, and it is a hard limit rather than a preference. GitHub
# refuses any single file over 100 megabytes, and pandoc.exe is well past
# that. Track it with Git LFS, or attach it to a release instead of
# committing it, and keep a local copy beside this file so the installer can
# pick it up. The installer skips it cleanly when it is absent.
pandoc.exe
